# rưỡi is "and a half", counted from the hour ALREADY NAMED -- the English
# "half past" direction, not the Germanic toward-the-hour one: the
# dictionary's own worked example is "ba (giờ) rưỡi chiều" == 3:30 PM.  It
# attaches with or without giờ, hence the optional hour word in the order.
# The same locale's kém counts the OTHER way (see clock_dir_to.voc); the
# direction is a property of the word here, not of the language.
# en.wiktionary.org, https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/r%C6%B0%E1%BB%A1i.
rưỡi
